            <div xml:id="d896">

                <pb facs="1321" n="1307" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/9–2048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Special Representative in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-20T19:00:00-04:00">September 20,
                            1948—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Fol press statement issued today by Dept response questions re attitude
                    toward announced Soviet decision withdraw occupation forces from Korea: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“It has been consistent view this govt that best interests Korean people
                            would be served by withdrawal all occupying forces from Korea earliest
                            practicable date. Same view embodied UN
                            GA Res Nov 14, 1947 in which provision
                            made for such withdrawal soon as practicable after establishment Korean
                            Govt which it was intention Res bring into being. Had Soviet Union
                            cooperated carrying out provisions Res Nov 14, 1947 question troop
                            withdrawal from Korea would doubtless have been already resolved.</p>
                        <p>“US Govt regards question withdrawal occupying forces as but one facet
                            entire question unity and independence Korea. GA of UN has taken
                            cognizance of this larger question, as evidenced by Res referred <pb
                                facs="1322" n="1308" xml:id="pg1308"/> to above and may be expected
                            give further consideration to matter at its forthcoming meeting.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
